      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): preserve full agent ID with colon in session key",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a session key contains multiple colons (e.g. `agent:my-agent:explicit:session123`), `.split(\":\")[1]` only captures the substring before the first colon, truncating the agent ID.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe `row.key.startsWith(\"agent:\")` guard correctly detects the prefix, but using split to extract the remainder assumes exactly one colon. Using `.slice(\"agent:\".length)` preserves the full ID after the prefix.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent display names in session listings may show truncated agent IDs for explicitly-named sessions with colons in the key.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore:\n```\nnode -e \"console.log('agent:my-agent:extra:session123'.split(':')[1])\"\n→ \"my-agent\" (truncated)\n```\n\nAfter:\n```\nnode -e \"const key = 'agent:my-agent:extra:session123'; console.log(key.startsWith('agent:') ? key.slice('agent:'.length) : undefined)\"\n→ \"my-agent:extra:session123\" (preserved)\n```\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n",
        "branch": "fix/sessions-agentid-colon",
